cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this repository, please cite it as below."
title: "FrugalAI: useful AI on the hardware people already have"
type: software
abstract: >-
  A collection of specific, working AI applications and the evidence behind them. Each one runs on the edge:
  a plain laptop with no good GPU, a Raspberry Pi or another small board, with no internet needed at run time.
  The aim is to address real problems of rural India and of people with the least access, and to make it cheap
  for students and small startups to build many more.
authors:
  - family-names: Kulkarni
    given-names: Yogesh Haribhau
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/yogeshhk/FrugalAI"
keywords:
  - frugal AI
  - edge AI
  - small language models
  - offline
  - Raspberry Pi
  - India
